// Shallow Nix grammar for flake.nix surgery (CST mode, -disable-spaces).
//
// FIRST of two passes. This grammar deliberately does NOT parse all of Nix.
// It parses just enough structure to navigate a flake.nix to its top-level
// `inputs` attrset and `outputs` binding, so conformist can splice new
// bindings in by byte offset while preserving the rest of the file verbatim.
// The `outputs` value is parsed opaquely here; the recognized
// eachDefaultSystem shape is parsed in a SECOND pass (outputs.peg) over the
// located value's byte range.
//
// Anything this grammar cannot parse makes Match fail, and the caller falls
// back to print-only rather than corrupting the file.
//
// Everything lexical — bindings, values, strings, comments, trivia, tokens —
// lives in shared.peg and is imported below; see its header for why those
// rules are defined exactly once (conformist#106). Being the FIRST pass, this
// file is upstream of outputs.peg: a disagreement between the two about where
// a value ENDS is the highest-consequence bug class in a tool that rewrites
// flake.nix in place.
//
// Ported from amarbel-llc/doppelgang internal/0/nixedit/nix.peg, which is
// itself modelled on amarbel-llc/langlang grammars/toml.peg.

@import Trivia, Binding, BraceOpen, BraceClose, EOF from "./shared.peg"

// ── Top-level ────────────────────────────────────────────────
// First rule is the PEG entry point (this file is the QueryMatcher
// entrypoint; imports do not displace it). A flake.nix is a single attribute
// set with optional surrounding trivia. We parse its bindings; each binding's
// key path is structured, its value opaque.

File       <- Trivia AttrSet Trivia EOF

AttrSet    <- BraceOpen Trivia Binding* BraceClose
